      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The idea that vitamin C \"cleanses\" kidneys is a common myth, but scientific evidence shows that high doses actually raise urinary oxalate levels, which can worsen existing stone formers or even trigger new ones. Once kidney stones develop, the kidneys become more prone to absorbing recycled calcium and oxalate, making high-dose supplementation dangerous rather than detoxifying. Please ignore internet myths on this topic and speak to a medical professional immediately about a safe, personalized plan to manage your condition.",
